  "step_3": "The decision reason requires calculating an aspiration level as the mean of all outcomes (3000 Euros) and comparing the probabilities that each lottery's outcomes exceed this level. The individual does not reference any such calculation or comparison. Instead, they focus solely on the probability of receiving any money (non-zero outcome) versus getting nothing. This reflects a 'chance of winning something' heuristic, not an aspiration-based evaluation involving outcome differences from a mean. There is no mention of 3000 as a reference, nor of evaluating which outcomes are above or below it. The justification is based on a different cognitive process — avoiding the high chance of getting nothing — rather than assessing positive deviations from an aspiration level. Therefore, the reasoning process described in the verbal report does not align with the specified decision reason in either information use or decision rule.",
